+# patches/
+
+Harness-side patches this plugin still needs. Each patch targets the pinned
+`dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2` checkout (`0a53fb55bea101816fa226bb964ae2bed71c343b`) and
+applies from its root with `git apply`.
+
+| Patch | Target | Why the plugin needs it |
+|---|---|---|
+| `dsh-composer-dock-hero.patch` | `packages/client/ui-conversation/src/client/skeleton/ConversationRoot.tsx` | Renders `conversation.composer.dock` on the hero (blank-session) composer as well as the docked one. The documented entry point of this plugin is that slot; the shell currently skips it with `!hero`, so the dock — and the live input handle it publishes — goes dark exactly in hero/blank mode, the mode the plugin's documented `apply`-level listener is there to cover. The `conversation.input.dock` bridge in `client.js` is the degrade for unpatched hosts; it is not a reason to drop the patch. |
+
+Applying the patch on the checkout (do not commit to the pinned checkout):
+
+```sh
+git -C .dsh-migrate/harness apply patches/dsh-composer-dock-hero.patch
+```
+
+Re-verified against the exact tag: `git apply --check` passes on the pristine
+`HEAD` file, and the checkout's working tree equals the patch result
+(`git apply --check -R` passes). The patch stays required — the hero bridge in
+`client.js` registers in `conversation.input.dock`, which is a different slot
+(full-width strip above the card), so it does not replace the documented
+`conversation.composer.dock` entry.
+
+A discussion draft for this patch lives at
+`.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/composer-dock-hero/report.md`.
